; Regression test for issue #3312: format samples whose bare symbol is
; still an error (3312.test has the samples that are now read).
;
; A bare symbol that meets the number between two number characters is
; not taken for the declared symbol, since nothing marks where it ends.
; The sample is parsed as written, so "N11,000.00" names N, and
; "1,000.001X" names X.  Quoting the symbol, or setting it off from the
; number with a space, removes the doubt.
commodity N1
    format N11,000.00

commodity 1X
    format 1,000.001X

; Only the declared symbol is recognized bare.
commodity N4
    format 1,000.00 N5

; A sample with no number.
commodity N6
    format N6

test bal -> 4
__ERROR__
While parsing file "$FILE", line 10:
Error: commodity directive symbol "N1" and format directive symbol N should be the same
While parsing file "$FILE", line 13:
Error: commodity directive symbol "1X" and format directive symbol X should be the same
While parsing file "$FILE", line 17:
Error: unexpected characters '5' after commodity symbol in format directive
While parsing file "$FILE", line 21:
Error: No quantity specified for amount
end test
